les fail to comply with the requirements of Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standard (FMVSS) number 111, \"Rear Visibility.\"","consequence":"The lack of an image in the back-up camera display increases the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Nissan will notify owners in phases, having dealers update the back-up camera settings software, free of charge.  The recall began November 11, 2019 and all affected VINs should be activated.  Owners may contact Nissan customer service at 1-800-867-7669 or INFINITI customer service at 1-800-662-6200.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":1228830,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=19V654000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":46,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2018","make":"INFINITI","model":"Q60"},{"year":"2018","make":"NISSAN","model":"MAXIMA"},{"year":"2018","make":"NISSAN","model":"TITAN"},{"year":"2018","make":"NISSAN","model":"SENTRA"},{"year":"2018","make":"NISSAN","model":"ROGUE"},{"year":"2018","make":"NISSAN","model":"NV200"},{"year":"2018","make":"INFINITI","model":"QX80"},{"year":"2019","make":"NISSAN","model":"MURANO"},{"year":"2019","make":"NISSAN","model":"MAXIMA"},{"year":"2019","make":"NISSAN","model":"TITAN"},{"year":"2019","make":"NISSAN","model":"GT-R"},{"year":"2019","make":"NISSAN","model":"PATHFINDER"},{"year":"2019","make":"NISSAN","model":"ROGUE"},{"year":"2019","make":"NISSAN","model":"NV"},{"year":"2018","make":"NISSAN","model":"ROGUE SPORT"},{"year":"2019","make":"NISSAN","model":"ROGUE SPORT"},{"year":"2019","make":"NISSAN","model":"SENTRA"},{"year":"2019","make":"NISSAN","model":"VERSA NOTE"},{"year":"2019","make":"NISSAN","model":"VERSA"},{"year":"2018","make":"NISSAN","model":"VERSA NOTE"},{"year":"2019","make":"INFINITI","model":"QX50"},{"year":"2018","make":"NISSAN","model":"LEAF"},{"year":"2019","make":"INFINITI","model":"QX60"},{"year":"2019","make":"NISSAN","model":"KICKS"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true},{"campaign":"19V807000","received":"2019-11-08","manufacturer":"Nissan North America, Inc.","component":"SERVICE BRAKES, HYDRAULIC:ANTILOCK/TRACTION CONTROL/ELECTRONIC LIMITED SLIP","summary":"Nissan North America, Inc. (Nissan) is recalling certain 2015-2018 Nissan Murano, 2016-2018 Nissan Maxima, and 2017-2019 Nissan Pathfinder and Infiniti QX60 vehicles.  These vehicles were previously recalled and unrepaired, or inspected and determined to not need a repair, under recall number 18V-601. In addition, this recall expands the previous population.  The Anti-lock Brake System (ABS) actuator pumps may allow brake fluid to leak onto an internal circuit board.","consequence":"A brake fluid leak on the circuit board may result in an electrical short, increasing the risk of a fire.","remedy":"Nissan will notify owners, and dealers will replace the ABS actuator, free of charge.  Owners will receive a second notice when remedy parts become available, currently expected to be during summer 2020.  Owners may contact Nissan customer service at 1-800-867-7669.  Note:  If the ABS warning light remains illuminated for more than 10 seconds after engine start up, owners are advised to park the vehicle outdoors away from other vehicles or structures and to not drive the vehicle.","park_it":false,"park_outside":true,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":391479,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=19V807000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":13,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2019","make":"NISSAN","model":"PATHFINDER"},{"year":"2016","make":"NISSAN","model":"MURANO"},{"year":"2018","make":"INFINITI","model":"QX60"},{"year":"2018","make":"NISSAN","model":"MAXIMA"},{"year":"2018","make":"NISSAN","model":"PATHFINDER"},{"year":"2017","make":"NISSAN","model":"MAXIMA"},{"ye